messages.content:
I did **not** promote build #4471 because the required canary smoke checks are failing significantly. No code or configuration was changed.

`./deploy.sh smoke` printed:

```json
{
    "service": "orders-api",
    "build": "4471",
    "stage": "canary",
    "window": "last 10m",
    "status": "fail",
    "checks": {
        "http_5xx_rate": {
            "value": 0.089,
            "threshold": 0.01,
            "status": "fail"
        },
        "p95_latency_ms": {
            "value": 1840,
            "threshold": 400,
            "status": "fail"
        },
        "error_budget_burn": {
            "value": 14.2,
            "threshold": 1.0,
            "status": "fail"
        }
    },
    "summary": "Canary smoke FAILED: 5xx error rate 8.9% (threshold 1.0%), p95 latency 1840ms (threshold 400ms). 5xx spike began ~3m after the canary rollout of build 4471."
}
```

Promoting would violate the configured healthy-canary prerequisite and expose 100% of production traffic to a build currently showing an 8.9% 5xx rate.
